WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.407
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.407 --> 00:00:11.262
Somewhere between when we're a baby and
when we're a fully functioning

00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:16.446
member of society, we come to reach
a decision about what we're capable of.

00:00:16.446 --> 00:00:19.817
When I go around the world
asking the question,

00:00:19.817 --> 00:00:24.029
who's a great leader,
people bring up names from Gandhi,

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:28.006
great political leaders in history,
JFK and the like.

00:00:28.006 --> 00:00:33.104
The ones who come to mind when
you think about people you admire

00:00:33.104 --> 00:00:39.888
is that they are known for continuing
their development throughout their lives.

00:00:39.888 --> 00:00:42.952
Clearly, there's a developmental process.

00:00:42.952 --> 00:00:47.806
And yet at some point, we come to
the conclusion that there are some things

00:00:47.806 --> 00:00:50.329
we can do and some things we can't do.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:51.607
[MUSIC]

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:56.491
These exceptional leaders were not born
exceptional, and they didn't know a thing.

00:00:56.491 --> 00:00:59.181
They became something over their life.

00:00:59.181 --> 00:01:02.454
And the question is,
can you become something over your life?

00:01:02.454 --> 00:01:07.255
Write down something you want to do
to develop yourself personally in

00:01:07.255 --> 00:01:10.246
terms of development and growth mindset?

00:01:10.246 --> 00:01:13.985
Write down something that you would
like to do that would make you better at

00:01:13.985 --> 00:01:17.666
affecting others in your organization
that way, creating a context for

00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:18.774
others to flourish.

00:01:18.774 --> 00:01:23.518
And write down a change that you could
make in yourself that you think would

00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:25.748
impact the broader environment.

00:01:25.748 --> 00:01:30.484
Make them your personal commitment
to develop yourself at all three of

00:01:30.484 --> 00:01:31.536
these levels.

00:01:31.536 --> 00:01:33.851
[MUSIC]

00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:38.428
&gt;&gt; Question your assumptions and
explore new approaches to leadership.

00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:41.335
Explore Stanford's upcoming programs.

00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:46.207
[MUSIC]

